{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"heavyset-fungiform-hartebeest","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Config schema + layered-merge core + capability descriptor (provider-neutral)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nThe reconciler's rebar↔Jira mappings are hardcoded literals in\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py`,\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/config.py`, and\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_fields.py`. Before any axis can become\nconfig-driven, the seam needs a provider-neutral foundation: a config schema, a layered\noverlay/merge, a fail-closed validation framework, and a capability descriptor that\ndeclares which axes a target has. This is the walking skeleton every other child in the\nepic depends on. It ships with **no axis wired yet** — it stands up the machinery and\nproves it, and S2–S5 move each axis onto it.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a provider-neutral module (new file\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mapping_config.py`) that:\n\n1. **Parses** an optional `[tool.rebar.jira]` mapping block from rebar's existing config\n   surface (per `docs/config.md`; keys under `reconciler.*`/`jira.*` are already routed\n   to consumers per bug fond-gloom-dingo). Shape: a `default` block and a\n   `projects.<KEY>` table, each carrying axis sub-tables (`status_map`, `type_map`,\n   `link_map`, `priority_map`, `create_defaults`) plus discovered-vocabulary lists\n   (`statuses`, `issue_types`, `link_types`, a `hierarchy` level map). Absent block ⇒\n   empty overlay (today's behavior).\n2. **Resolves** an effective mapping for a given project key by deep per-key merge:\n   built-in default (injected by the caller — the adapter's constants) ← `default`\n   block ← `projects.<KEY>`. Per-key means an overlay `status_map` entry overrides only\n   that status; unnamed keys inherit.\n3. **Validates** fail-closed at load: a mapped value must appear in the project's\n   declared vocabulary set when one is declared (e.g. every `status_map` value ∈\n   `statuses`); a value referencing an axis the capability descriptor marks absent is\n   rejected; malformed blocks raise rather than degrade. Validation is **offline** — it\n   reads only config, never the network.\n4. Defines a **`Capability` descriptor** dataclass (which axes exist: `has_types`,\n   `has_transitions`, `has_hierarchy`, `has_link_types`, …) so \"target lacks this axis\"\n   flows through the same skip/drift paths a missing value does.\n\nThe module imports nothing from the Jira adapter (provider-neutral); the adapter injects\nits built-in defaults and capability values. This respects the ADR 0035 one-way\ndependency direction (`_backend.py`: concrete backends import shared/core, never the\nreverse).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mapping_config.py` (new) — schema dataclasses,\n  `load_mapping_config`, `resolve_for_project`, `validate`, `Capability`.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_mapping_config.py` (new) — merge, validation,\n  neutrality tests.\n- `docs/config.md` — document the `[tool.rebar.jira]` mapping block shape and merge\n  semantics (leaf-level doc of the new keys).\n\n## Testing\n\n- **Unit (in-process, real function):** deep-merge precedence — assert a\n  `projects.REB.status_map` entry wins over `default.status_map` which wins over an\n  injected built-in default, and an unnamed key falls through all three.\n- **Config-effect contrast:** resolve at the built-in default and at a non-default\n  overlay value and assert the effective map differs exactly as specified (guards the\n  read-but-miswired class).\n- **Fail-closed validation (failure path):** a `status_map` value not in the declared\n  `statuses` set raises a named error; a malformed block raises; an axis-absent\n  reference raises — each asserted on the exact error, with the nearest valid config as\n  the negative control (must NOT raise).\n- **Neutrality:** assert `mapping_config` has no import of any `adapters.jira*` module\n  and contains no Jira value literal (e.g. `\"To Do\"`, `\"Initiative\"`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `load_mapping_config` parses a `default` + `projects.<KEY>` block with the five\n  axis sub-tables and the vocabulary lists; an absent block yields an empty overlay —\n  verified by `test_mapping_config.py::test_absent_block_is_empty_overlay`.\n- [ ] `resolve_for_project` deep-merges per key with precedence built-in ← default ←\n  project — verified by `test_mapping_config.py::test_perkey_merge_precedence` (asserts\n  overridden key changes, unnamed key inherits).\n- [ ] A non-default overlay produces a different effective mapping than the built-in\n  default through the real resolve path — verified by\n  `test_mapping_config.py::test_config_effect_contrast`.\n- [ ] `validate` fails closed offline on: a value outside the declared vocabulary, a\n  malformed block, and a reference to a capability-absent axis; the nearest valid config\n  does not raise — verified by `test_mapping_config.py::test_validate_fails_closed`.\n- [ ] The core is provider-neutral: `mapping_config` imports no `adapters.jira*` module\n  and carries no Jira value literal — verified by\n  `test_mapping_config.py::test_core_is_provider_neutral`.\n- [ ] `docs/config.md` documents the mapping block shape and merge semantics.\n\nTest tier: **in-process unit** — the mechanism is pure config parse/merge/validate over\nreal functions; no external boundary is crossed, so a lower tier is impossible and a\nhigher (subprocess/live) tier would not cross any additional component.","id":"bfe7-0900-c3d1-4141","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","priority":2,"tags":["reconciler","config","mapping-seam"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Config schema + layered-merge core + capability descriptor (provider-neutral)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787287206477113001,"uuid":"77c69d5c-0c5b-4348-9ff2-cec05907414c"}